# Fetched at build time by scripts/fetch-vendor.sh, not committed: the model is
# 10.4 MB, it is a swappable art asset, and every re-export of it would cost
# every clone another 10.4 MB forever.
#
# First non-comment line is the base URL. Every line after it is a filename,
# which must also appear in SHA256SUMS: the pin is the contract, this file only
# says where to get the bytes. Bump the commit here and the hash there
# together, and say in the commit message where the bytes came from.
#
# Two fields because this tree serves the model as jim.vrm and upstream calls it
# Seed-san.vrm. Pinned to a commit rather than to master: master is a branch and
# would move under the hash, which turns a silent substitution into a fetch that
# fails and names both hashes, but only after someone waits for 10.4 MB.
#
# three-vrm.js is not here on purpose. It is built locally with pinned esbuild
# from the recipe in README.md, so there is no URL to fetch it from; it stays
# committed and SHA256SUMS still pins it.
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vrm-c/vrm-specification/837f156dbce43ad69183ce1bdab549961ae1c1ee/samples/Seed-san/vrm/
jim.vrm Seed-san.vrm
